WEBVTT

1
00:00:09.904 --> 00:00:15.747
Plumfield School, dedicated to the memory of Elizabeth March, opened its doors three months later.

2
00:00:17.048 --> 00:00:22.490
People came from town and from neighboring cities near and far to satisfy their curiosity about the new

3
00:00:22.530 --> 00:00:25.992
establishment. "It's a nice turnout, isn't it?"

4
00:00:26.336 --> 00:00:31.920
Mr. Laurence said proudly as he waved at a few familiar faces and warmly greeted those he didn't

5
00:00:32.020 --> 00:00:32.600
know as well.

6
00:00:34.101 --> 00:00:39.305
Mother kept wiping tears from her eyes as she said over and over again, "Beth would be so

7
00:00:39.385 --> 00:00:46.890
happy." Jo, along with Amy and Laurie, happily served drinks and snacks to the visitors and directed all

8
00:00:46.950 --> 00:00:49.091
those who had questions to Professor Bauer.

9
00:00:50.052 --> 00:00:54.715
Meg gave tours of the place while John minded the children and made sure they didn't eat more

10
00:00:54.815 --> 00:00:55.836
cookies than they should.

11
00:00:57.468 --> 00:01:03.950
"I desperately need a cold drink," the Professor gasped as he politely detached himself from a group of

12
00:01:04.010 --> 00:01:08.271
mothers who had gathered to pepper him with questions about the school curriculum.

13
00:01:09.251 --> 00:01:13.852
Handing him a tall glass of lemonade, Jo asked, "Do you think it's going to be a success?"

14
00:01:15.433 --> 00:01:20.134
Looking at her tenderly, the Professor remarked, "Jo, whatever you do will succeed.

15
00:01:20.754 --> 00:01:21.414
Do you know why?"

16
00:01:22.355 --> 00:01:26.896
Without waiting for an answer, he replied, "Because you put your whole soul into it."

17
00:01:27.572 --> 00:01:32.817
Laurie and Amy exchanged knowing glances as they predicted another wedding in the March family soon.

18
00:01:34.718 --> 00:01:39.362
At present, however, the Professor's very words, like a prophecy, were about to come true.

19
00:01:40.283 --> 00:01:45.047
A young delivery boy ran up to the refreshment table asking for Josephine March.

20
00:01:45.067 --> 00:01:47.629
"That's me," she replied.

21
00:01:47.649 --> 00:01:51.573
"Package for you, ma'am," the boy said, handing her a thick envelope.

22
00:01:51.593 --> 00:01:53.895
"What is it, Jo?"

23
00:01:54.275 --> 00:01:55.336
Amy asked curiously.

24
00:01:56.148 --> 00:01:59.491
"I don't know," Jo said as she ripped the envelope open.

25
00:02:00.672 --> 00:02:05.556
Inside was a bound book, and when Jo saw the title and author's name, she let out a

26
00:02:05.616 --> 00:02:08.698
cry, "It's my novel!"

27
00:02:10.219 --> 00:02:14.343
The Professor caught her arm to steady her while Amy took the book from Jo's hands.

28
00:02:14.363 --> 00:02:20.768
"The Little Women: A Story About Life, by Jo March," she read.

29
00:02:20.788 --> 00:02:23.650
"Jo! This is your book!

30
00:02:23.910 --> 00:02:25.532
Your book's been published!"

31
00:02:26.348 --> 00:02:31.970
Hearing Amy's excited voice and Laurie's cheers, Meg came running, followed by their parents.

32
00:02:32.890 --> 00:02:37.391
When Laurie held up the book, everyone clapped and shouted their congratulations loudly.

33
00:02:37.411 --> 00:02:41.873
"See, Jo, another success," whispered the Professor.

34
00:02:41.893 --> 00:02:46.434
"Your soul is in that book, just as it is in this school."

35
00:02:47.254 --> 00:02:52.256
Jo took his hand without saying a word, because he already knew what she wanted to say.

36
00:02:53.224 --> 00:02:57.125
The grand opening of the school brought greater results than anyone had thought.

37
00:02:59.086 --> 00:03:04.568
It was obvious that the upcoming days would be busy with accepting applications and planning lessons.

38
00:03:05.608 --> 00:03:09.050
John quit his job and took on a position as an English teacher.

39
00:03:10.050 --> 00:03:15.332
Amy volunteered to work part-time as the art instructor, and Meg said she would teach a sewing class.

40
00:03:16.688 --> 00:03:21.971
Aside from the other teachers who were hired, Plumfield School was the joint effort of the March, Laurence,

41
00:03:22.011 --> 00:03:23.992
and Brookes families uniting as one.

42
00:03:25.292 --> 00:03:29.654
As she pondered that, Jo decided it would be a good chance for her to spend some private

43
00:03:29.694 --> 00:03:30.635
time with her sisters.

44
00:03:31.415 --> 00:03:34.997
They agreed to take a walk together, just the three of them, down to the pond.

45
00:03:35.017 --> 00:03:41.160
"This has really been an eventful day," Meg said when they reached the pond and sat on a

46
00:03:41.200 --> 00:03:41.760
fallen log.

47
00:03:43.260 --> 00:03:46.622
"My legs are killing me," said Amy, rubbing her sore feet.

48
00:03:46.642 --> 00:03:51.325
"But I'd gladly stand for weeks if it means making this school a success."

49
00:03:52.305 --> 00:03:57.088
The girls sat together watching a few ducks swim around the pond as the sun was sinking in

50
00:03:57.108 --> 00:03:57.568
the sky.

51
00:03:58.789 --> 00:04:02.811
"We used to come out here a lot when we were younger, but I haven't been for so

52
00:04:02.891 --> 00:04:04.012
long," said Meg.

53
00:04:04.032 --> 00:04:09.615
"Remember how we used to swim in the water, and Jo would grab our legs and try to

54
00:04:09.675 --> 00:04:10.395
pull us under?"

55
00:04:10.756 --> 00:04:11.356
giggled Amy.

56
00:04:12.024 --> 00:04:16.648
"Then you'd run home and tell Mother or Father what I did and get me in trouble," Jo

57
00:04:16.708 --> 00:04:17.228
pointed out.

58
00:04:17.248 --> 00:04:22.132
"We were so young and carefree," Amy said with a smile on her face.

59
00:04:22.152 --> 00:04:28.096
"That's why we did so many foolish things," Meg said, blushing at the memory of some of her

60
00:04:28.156 --> 00:04:29.057
embarrassing moments.

61
00:04:29.077 --> 00:04:32.159
"But look at us now, girls," said Jo.

62
00:04:32.179 --> 00:04:34.581
"Meg is a mother with two children.

63
00:04:35.081 --> 00:04:38.284
Amy is married to Laurie and may soon start a family of her own."

64
00:04:39.192 --> 00:04:44.894
"And Jo is an accomplished writer and headmistress of the most prestigious school in America," Amy added with

65
00:04:44.954 --> 00:04:50.497
pride. "By the way, you never told us what your book is about, Jo," said Meg.

66
00:04:51.257 --> 00:04:57.479
Looking out at the pond, Jo took a moment to gather her thoughts before answering, "It's about dreams

67
00:04:57.539 --> 00:05:06.223
and failures, growing up and growing pains, love and heartache, opportunities and memories, regrets and hope, birth and

68
00:05:06.303 --> 00:05:08.444
death It's about life."

69
00:05:09.620 --> 00:05:14.123
The sisters grew silent as they watched the sun slowly disappear below the horizon.

70
00:05:14.143 --> 00:05:20.368
"I miss her so much," Amy said, choking up as her mind filled with memories of Beth.

71
00:05:21.549 --> 00:05:25.711
As they used to do when they were younger, the girls wrapped their arms around each other and

72
00:05:25.771 --> 00:05:31.656
cried. "Beth wouldn't want us to cry every time we think of her," sniffed Amy.

73
00:05:31.676 --> 00:05:34.598
"You're right," Meg said, wiping her eyes.

74
00:05:34.618 --> 00:05:39.713
"Beth was always a positive, happy girl, and that's how I want to remember her."

75
00:05:39.733 --> 00:05:45.375
"Remember how she used to always get excited whenever we started a new chapter in a book?"

76
00:05:45.775 --> 00:05:46.256
asked Jo.

77
00:05:47.816 --> 00:05:53.479
Giggling at the memory, Amy said, "She said new chapters are the best because there is so much

78
00:05:53.539 --> 00:05:54.559
to look forward to."

79
00:05:55.720 --> 00:05:57.841
Jo dried her eyes and looked at her sisters.

80
00:05:58.721 --> 00:05:59.761
"What do you say, girls?

81
00:06:00.602 --> 00:06:05.384
Let's tell each other about the new chapters in our lives that are about to begin," she suggested.

82
00:06:06.740 --> 00:06:07.761
Meg started first.

83
00:06:07.781 --> 00:06:11.323
"My new chapter begins with Daisy and Demi starting school.

84
00:06:13.324 --> 00:06:18.086
While they learn how to become good citizens, I will learn how to be a better mother, wife,

85
00:06:18.347 --> 00:06:19.687
daughter, and sister."

86
00:06:19.707 --> 00:06:25.971
"My new chapter begins with finding a house for me and Laurie to live in," said Amy, and

87
00:06:26.011 --> 00:06:27.331
laughed along with her sisters.

88
00:06:27.352 --> 00:06:32.975
"Then each day I want to do something that will touch the life of another person in some

89
00:06:33.035 --> 00:06:39.490
way, whether through my words, actions, instructions as a teacher, or even through my paintings."

90
00:06:40.631 --> 00:06:41.912
Finally it was Jo's turn.

91
00:06:41.932 --> 00:06:48.615
"My new chapter begins with the start of a new outlook on life, on relationships, on goals, and

92
00:06:48.815 --> 00:06:49.496
on myself.

93
00:06:50.476 --> 00:06:55.479
I hope to treasure each moment as it deserves to be valued and love each person as they

94
00:06:55.539 --> 00:06:56.579
deserve to be loved."

95
00:06:57.600 --> 00:07:02.463
Hugging each other tightly, the March sisters were grateful for each other and for the chance to bond

96
00:07:02.523 --> 00:07:04.904
even more closely as they grew older together.

97
00:07:06.528 --> 00:07:11.830
"Well, girls, it looks as if this day is almost over," said Amy, looking up at the darkening

98
00:07:11.890 --> 00:07:17.173
sky. "A new day waits for us tomorrow," said Meg, standing up to leave.

99
00:07:18.093 --> 00:07:23.895
As Jo followed her sisters back to the house, she added, "and a new chapter in this story

100
00:07:23.955 --> 00:07:24.596
called life."
